Coi.

I gave up learning lojban a while ago because I didn't have anyone I would 
be able to learn it with, but recently I got some new friends who want to 
learn. I decided that at the start I would teach them to speak saying every 
terminator so that we get used to the idea of them being there, however I 
noticed that it is inconsistent as to whether or not la is terminated by ku 
or if it has no terminator. For example in la camxes grammar parser adding 
a ku to the end of a sumti starting with la generates an error unless you 
use the experimental grammar version. My question therefore is, is using ku 
as a terminator experimental? and should I teach them that it is the 
terminator for la, or shouldn't I?

Thanks :)

-- 
